      "credits": 3,
      "syllabus": "Course Objectives:\n\nThe objective of this course is:\n• To understand and apply fundamental laws in D.C. electrical circuits.\n• To understand the magnetic circuits and the principle of operation of a transformer.\n• To acquire the required knowledge about DC machines and Induction motors.\n• To understand the characteristics of the Diode, the Transistor and their applications.\n• To analyze various configurations of the BUT, FET.\n\nUNIT-I: 12Hrs\n\nElectrical Circuits\nBasic definitions, types of elements, Ohm's Law, Kirchhoff’s Laws, resistive networks, series, parallel circuits,\nVoltage and Current division rules, Mesh analysis, Node Analysis, and Simple problems.\n\nUNIT-II: Magnetic Circuits &Transformer 12Hrs\n\nMagnetic circuits: Faraday’s laws of Electromagnetic Induction, Lenz’s Law, and Fleming’s right-hand Rule\nand left-hand Rule. Magnetic Circuits - Concept of Self-Inductance& Mutual Inductance, Coefficient of\nCoupling.\n\nTransformers: Construction, Basic Working Principle, EMF Equation, Applications, Simple Problems.\n\nUNIT-III: Electrical Machines 13Hrs\n\nDC Generators: Construction, Basic Working Principle, EMF Equation, Types of DC Generators, Applications,\nSimple Problems.\n\nDC Motors: Basic Working Principle, Types of DC Motors, Torque Equation, Speed Control of DC Shunt\nMotor, Applications, Simple Problems.\n\nSingle-phase Induction Machines:Principles of Operation of 1-phase Induction Motors, Capacitor Start\nMotors, Capacitor Start-Capacitor Run Motors, and Stepper Motors, Applications.\n\nUNIT-IV: Diode and Transistor 11Hrs\n\nDiode: p-n junction diode, V-I characteristics, Zener diode, Diode Applications, Rectifier-Half wave, Full wave\nand Bridge rectifier.\nTransistor: PNP and NPN junction transistor, Transistor as an amplifier.\n\nUNIT-V: 12Hrs\n\nBipolar Junction Transistor (BJT): Construction, Principle of Operation, Amplifying Action, Common Emitter,\nCommon Base and Common Collector configurations, Comparison of CE,CB and CC configurations.\n\nField Effect Transistor (FET): Construction, Principle of Operation, Comparison of BUT and FET, Biasing\nFET.",
      "textbooks": "1. Principles of Electrical and Electronics Engineering -V.K.Mehta, S.Chand& Co, 12\" Edition, 2019.\n2. Basic Electrical and Electronics Engineering -D P Kothari, | J Nagrath, McGraw-Hill Education, 2\"4\nEdition, 2020",
      "referenceBooks": "1. A Text book of Electrical Technology, Vol 2 — B.L. Thereja and A.K. Theraja, S. Chand Publications,\nreprint 2015.\n2. M.S.Sukhija, T.K.Nagsarkar, “Basic Electrical and Electronics Engineering”, paperback Edition, 2017.\n3. Electrical and Electronics Technology” — Hughes, Pearson Education, 12th Edition, 2016.",
      "outcomes": "After the completion of the course student should be able to\nCO-1. Analyse and solve electrical circuits using network laws.\n\nCO-2. Analyse Magnetic circuits and understand working of Transformers.\nCO-3. Understand the working principles of Electrical Machines.\n\nCO-4. Identify and characterize diodes and various types of transistors.\n\nCO-5. Understand different configurations of BUT, FET."
