      "outcomes": "After completion of the Course, the student should be able to\n\nCO-1. Apply fundamental data structure concepts to implement and utilize linear lists, stacks, and queues\nalong with their operations and applications.\n\nCO-2. Construct and traverse various tree structures, perform operations on BSTs, and apply balanced trees\nlike AVL and Red-Black trees in solving computational problems.\n\nCO-3. Implement multi-way search trees, B-Trees, B+ Trees, and heaps, and apply advanced searching\ntechniques such as interpolation and jump search for efficient problem solving.\n\nCO-4. Apply graph ADT in real-world applications, and implement efficient sorting techniques, including\nRadix, Heap, Merge, and Quick sort.\n\nCO-5. Design and implement hash tables using various hash functions and resolve collisions efficiently\nthrough chaining and open addressing techniques."
