      "credits": 1,
      "syllabus": "Course Objectives:\nThe objectives of this course are:\n• To analyze a given network by applying various electrical laws.\n• To understand magnetic circuits.\n• To study the performance characteristics of DC Machines.\n• To understand the Diode applications.\n• To study the input and output characteristics of BJT&FET.\n\nList of Experiments/ Demonstrations:\nPART A: ELECTRICAL (Compulsory)\n1. Verification of KVL and KCL.\n2. Measurement of Voltage, Current and Real Power in Primary and Secondary Circuits of a\nSingle-Phase Transformer.\n3. Magnetization Characteristics of DC Shunt Generator.\n4. Determination of self, mutual inductances and Coefficient of Coupling.\n5. Speed control of DC shunt Motor.\nPART B: ELECTRONICS (Compulsory)\n1. PN Junction diode characteristics.\n2. Zener diode characteristics and Zener as a voltage Regulator.\n3. Input & Output characteristics of Transistor in CB / CE configuration.\n4. Half-Wave and Full-Wave Rectifier without filters.\n5. Input and Output characteristics of FET in CS configuration.\nSelf-Practice Programs:\n\n1. Study of Voltage, Current and Power using Digital Energy Meter.\n2. Verification of Faraday’s Laws of Electromagnetic Induction.\n\n3. Load Test on DC Motor.\n\n4. Construction of AND & OR Gates using Diodes.\n\n5. Drain and Transfer Characteristics of MOSFET.",
