      "code": "2505204",
      "name": "Data Structures Laboratory",
      "l": 0,
      "t": 0,
      "p": 2,
      "credits": 1,
      "syllabus": "Course Objectives:\n• To develop the ability to implement and manipulate Singly and Circular Linked Lists, including\ncreation, insertion, deletion, and traversal using functions.\n• To implement different tree data structures and explore both recursive and non-recursive traversal\n\ntechniques.\n\n• To apply searching algorithms such as Interpolation Search and Jump Search for efficient data\nretrieval.\n\n• To apply sorting techniques, including Radix Sort, Heap Sort, Merge Sort, and Quick Sort, for ordering\ndatasets.\n\n• To understand and implement hash functions (Division, Multiplication, Mid-square methods) and\nhandle collisions effectively for efficient data storage and retrieval.\n\nList of Experiments:\n\n1. Write a program that uses functions to perform the following operations on Singly Linked List.\n\ni) Creation ii) Insertion iii) Deletion iv) Traversal\n2. Write a program that uses functions to perform the following operations on Circular Single Linked List.\ni) Creation ii) Insertion iii) Deletion iv) Traversal\n3. Write a program that implement Stack (its operations) using\ni) Arrays ii) ADT\n4. Write a program that implement Queue (its operations) using\ni) Arrays ii) ADT\n\n5. Write a program to implement the tree traversal methods (Recursive and Non-Recursive).\n6. Write a program to implement\n\ni) Binary Search tree ii) Binary Trees\n7. Write a program to implement\ni) Interpolation Search ii) Jump Search.\n\n8. Write a program to implement the graph traversal methods.\n9. Write a program that implements the following sorting methods to sort a given list of integers\nin ascending order\ni) Radix Sort ii) Heap sort iii) Merge Sort iv) Quick Sort.\n10. Write a program to implement the following Hash Functions:\ni) Division Method, ii) Multiplication Method iii) Mid-square Method.\n\nSelf-Practice Programs:\n\n1. Priority Queue using Binary Heap, Pattern Matching using Z-Algorithm\n2. Deque (Double Ended Queue) using Circular Array,\n\n3. Threaded Binary Tree,\n\n4. Expression Tree Construction & Evaluation\n\n5. Pattern Matching using Z-Algorithm",
      "textbooks": "1. Fundamentals of Data Structures in C, 2nd Edition, E. Horowitz, S. Sahni and Susan\nAnderson Freed, Universities Press.\n2. Data Structures using C — A. S. Tanenbaum, Y. Langsam, and M. J. Augenstein, PHI/Pearson\nEducation",
      "referenceBooks": "",
      "outcomes": "After completion of the Course, the student should be able to\nCO-1. Implement and manipulate Singly and Circular Linked Lists using functions for creation, insertion,\ndeletion, and traversal.\nCO-2. Construct and perform operations on Binary Trees and Binary Search Trees (BST) to solve\ncomputational problems.\n\nCO-3. Apply efficient searching algorithms, including Interpolation Search and Jump Search, to retrieve data\nfrom datasets.\n\nCO-4. To apply sorting techniques, including Radix Sort, Heap Sort, Merge Sort, and Quick Sort, for ordering\ndatasets.\n\nCO-5. Implement hash functions using Division, Multiplication, and Mid-square methods, and handle\ncollisions effectively for efficient data management."
