      "syllabus": "Course Objectives:\n• To introduce the fundamentals of object-oriented programming, Java basics, data types, operators,\ncontrol structures, and classes.\n• To understand the principles of inheritance, polymorphism, packages, and interfaces.\n• To learn exception handling, multithreading, synchronization, and inter-thread communication.\n• To explore Java libraries, event handling, and GUI fundamentals using AWT.\n• To develop applications using Swing components with MVC architecture.\n\nUNIT -I 12 Hrs\n\nObject-oriented thinking and Java Basics- Data types, variables, scope and lifetime of variables, arrays,\noperators, expressions, control statements, type conversion and casting, concepts of classes, objects,\nconstructors, methods, access control, this keyword, garbage collection, overloading methods and\nconstructors, parameter passing, recursion, nested classes.\n\nUNIT — II 12. Hrs\n\nInheritance, Packages and Interfaces — Hierarchical abstractions, Base class object, subclass, subtype,\nsubstitutability, construction, benefits of inheritance. super keyword uses, using the final keyword with\ninheritance, polymorphism- method overriding, abstract classes, the Object class. Defining, Creating and\nAccessing a Package, Understanding CLASSPATH, importing packages, differences between classes and\ninterfaces, defining an interface, implementing interface, applying interfaces.\n\nUNIT - Ill 12 Hrs\n\nException handling and Multithreading-- exception hierarchy, usage of try, catch, throw, throws, and finally,\nbuilt-in exceptions, creating own exception subclasses. Differences between multithreading and multitasking,\nthread life cycle, creating threads, thread priorities, synchronizing threads, and inter-thread communication.\n\nUNIT -IV 12 Hrs\nExploring String class, Object class, Exploring java.io package Event Handling: Events, Event sources, Event\nclasses, Event Listeners, Delegation event model, handling mouse and keyboard events, Adapter classes.\ngraphics, layout manager — layout manager types — border, grid, flow.\n\nUNIT-V 12 Hrs\nSwing — Introduction, limitations of AWT, MVC architecture, components, containers, exploring swing- JFrame\n\nand JComponent, JLabel, Imagelcon, JTextField, JButton, JCheckBox, JRadioButton, JList, JComboBox,\nTabbed Panes, Scroll Panes.",
