      "credits": 1,
      "syllabus": "Course Objectives:\n• Implement static and dynamic web pages using HTML, CSS, and Bootstrap, and perform client-side\nvalidation using JavaScript.\n• To develop an end-to-end application using a full-stack Java.\n• Introduce server-side programming using Node.js and Express.\n• Design and interact with databases using Java and MongoDB.\n• Explore single-page application (SPA) development using React.\n\nList of Experiments\n\n1. Build a responsive web application for a shopping cart with registration, login, catalog, and cart pages\nusing CSS3 features, flex, and grid.\n\n2. Make the above web application responsive using the Bootstrap framework.\n\n3. Use JavaScript for client-side validation of the pages implemented in exercises 1 and 2.\n\n4. Explore the features of ES6 like arrow functions, callbacks, promises, and async/await. Implement an\napplication to read weather information from openweathermap.org and display it as a graph on the\nweb page using Chart.js.\n\n5. Develop a Java standalone application that connects with the database (Oracle / MySQL) and\nperforms the CRUD operation on the database tables.\n\n6. Create an XML for the bookstore. Validate the same using both DTD and XSD.\n\n7. Create a custom server using the http module and explore other Node.js modules like OS, path, and\nevent.\n\n8. Develop an Express web application that connects to a MySQL database and performs CRUD\noperations on database tables. (Use Postman to test)\n\n9. Explore session tracking mechanisms (Cookies, HTTP Session) in Node.js using express-session and\ncookie-parser.\n\n10. For the above application, create authorized endpoints using JWT (JSON Web Token).\n\n11. Create a React application for the student management system,having registration, login, contact, and\nabout pages, and implement routing to navigate through these pages.\n\n12. Create a TODO application in Django with necessary components and deploy it to GitHub.\n\nSelf-Practice Programs:\n\n1. Progressive Web Apps development, Advanced CSS animations and transitions\n\n2. Modular JavaScript using ES modules and Webpack/Babel toolchain, Real-time web\ncommunication using WebSockets\n\n3.Server-side rendering (SSR) with Next.js for React apps, Component testing with Jest and\nReact Testing Library\n\n4.Integrating MongoDB / NoSQL databases alongside relational databases\n\n5.HTTPS, SSL certificates, and secure cookie handling, Integration of APIs for live data updates\n(stock, weather, news)",
