      "outcomes": "After completion of the Course, the student should be able to\n\nCO-1. Use Linux system calls for low-level file and process management.\n\nCO-2. Implement and analyze CPU scheduling algorithms (FCFS, SJF, Round Robin, Priority).\n\nCO-3. Implement deadlock-avoidance algorithms such as the Banker’s algorithm.\n\nCO-4. Apply synchronization mechanisms to solve Producer-Consumer and IPC problems.\n\nCO-5. Simulate memory management techniques (Paging, Segmentation) and page replacement policies\n(FIFO, LRU)."
