      "credits": 1,
      "syllabus": "Course Objectives:\n• To enable effective use of Business Intelligence (Bl) technology (Power BI) for data visualization.\n• To discern patterns and relationships in datasets.\n• To design and develop interactive Dashboards and Reports.\n• To communicate insights clearly and concisely using visual tools.\n• To work with multiple data formats and sources within Power Bl\n\nList of Experiments\n\n1. Understanding Data: What is data, where to find data, foundations for building data visualizations,\ncreating your first visualization in Power BI.\n\n2. Getting started with Power BI: Understanding data file formats, connecting your data to Power BI,\ncreating basic charts (line, bar charts, tree maps), and using the visualization pane.\n\n3. Power BI Calculations: Overview of SUM, AVERAGE, and aggregate functions, creating custom\ncalculations and fields using DAX (Data Analysis Expressions).\n\n4. Applying new calculations to your visualizations: Formatting visualizations, using formatting tools and\nmenus, and formatting specific parts of the visual.\n\n5. Editing and formatting axes, transforming data in Power Query, pivoting/unpivoting data.\n\n6. Structuring your data: Sorting and filtering in Power BI, managing relationships between tables.\n\n7. Advanced Visualization Tools: Using filters, the Details pane, the Size well, customizing filters,\ntooltips, and applying conditional formatting with colors.\n\n8. Creating Dashboards & Storytelling: Building your first dashboard and report, designing for different\ndisplay sizes, adding interactivity, and publishing your reports to Power BI Service.\n\n9. Power BI file types, sharing your reports and dashboards, exporting to PDF or PowerPoint, and\nprinting visuals.\n\n10. Creating custom visuals, working with time-series data, dual-axis charts, and advanced chart types\navailable in Power BI.\n\nSelf-Practice Programs:\n\n1. Advanced DAX Functions\nCompare multiple data sets using DAX.\n2. Power BI Advanced Analytics\nPerform statistical analysis using Power BI (e.g., correlation, regression, percentiles).\n3. Real-time Data Visualization\nConnect Power BI to real-time streaming datasets (loT sensors, Twitter feeds, APIs).\n4. Row-level Security (RLS)\nImplement security at the data row level based on user roles.\n5. Advanced Custom Visuals\nUse custom visuals from Microsoft AppSource or develop your own using R or Python scripts.",
